          "java",
          "FormValidator validator = new FormValidator();\nvalidator.addValidation(\"email\", s -> s.contains(\"@\") && s.contains(\".\"));\nvalidator.addValidation(\"password\", s -> s.length() >= 8);\nvalidator.addValidation(\"age\", s -> {\n    try { int age = Integer.parseInt(s); return age >= 18 && age <= 120; }\n    catch (NumberFormatException e) { return false; }\n});\n\nMap<String, String> form = Map.of(\"email\", \"test@example.com\", \"password\", \"short\", \"age\", \"25\");\nList<String> errors = validator.getErrors(form);\n// [password is invalid]"
